{"issue":{"title":"Add a --shout option to greet that prints the greeting in upper case, and document it in docs/","problem":"greet has no shout mode. bin/greet.js takes the first argument that does not start with '--' as the name and quietly ignores every '--' flag. So right now `node bin/greet.js --shout Ann` prints `Hello, Ann!` and exits 0, exactly like `node bin/greet.js Ann`. The flag is accepted but does nothing. docs/index.md, the source of the published docs site (the .github/workflows/pages.yml workflow uploads docs/ on every push to main), describes only `node bin/greet.js <name>` and never mentions --shout.","reason":"Support staff want a louder greeting for the lobby screen, and they need a docs page they can send people to that explains the option.","outcome":"`greet --shout <name>` prints the normal greeting in upper case and plain `greet <name>` works as before. docs/index.md documents --shout, so once the PR is merged to main the existing pages workflow publishes it to https://o.github.io/greet-cli/.","expect":["`node bin/greet.js --shout Ann` writes exactly `HELLO, ANN!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","`node bin/greet.js Ann --shout` writes exactly `HELLO, ANN!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","`node bin/greet.js Ann` without --shout still writes exactly `Hello, Ann!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","`node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with code 2 and writes nothing to stdout","docs/index.md documents the --shout option: it shows how to use it with a name and says that it prints the greeting in upper case","`npm test` exits 0, and test/greet.test.js has at least one test that runs the CLI with --shout and checks for upper-case output"],"proofs":[{"line":"`node bin/greet.js --shout Ann` writes exactly `HELLO, ANN!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js --shout Ann | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"   # expect H E L L O ,   A N N ! \\n and exit=0"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js Ann --shout` writes exactly `HELLO, ANN!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ann --shout | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"   # expect HELLO, ANN!\\n and exit=0"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js Ann` without --shout still writes exactly `Hello, Ann!` plus a newline to stdout and exits 0","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ann | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"   # expect Hello, Ann!\\n and exit=0"},{"line":"`node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with code 2 and writes nothing to stdout","proof":"run","how":"out=$(node bin/greet.js --shout 2>/dev/null); echo \"exit=$? stdout=[$out]\"   # expect exit=2 stdout=[]"},{"line":"docs/index.md documents the --shout option: it shows how to use it with a name and says that it prints the greeting in upper case","proof":"read","how":"Read docs/index.md at the PR head. Check for a usage example that includes --shout and a name, and a statement that the greeting comes out in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, <NAME>!`)."},{"line":"`npm test` exits 0, and test/greet.test.js has at least one test that runs the CLI with --shout and checks for upper-case output","proof":"run","how":"npm test; echo \"exit=$?\" (expect 0). Then grep -n -- '--shout' test/greet.test.js and read the matching test to confirm it runs bin/greet.js with --shout and asserts upper-case output."}],"non_goals":["Deploying or checking the live docs site at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/. That happens after merge through the existing pages workflow, which this issue does not change.","Changing .github/workflows/pages.yml.","Adding other flags, or changing the greeting text in normal mode.","Rejecting unknown flags or changing the usage message."],"assumptions":["'Louder' means the whole greeting in upper case: `Hello, Ann!` becomes `HELLO, ANN!`, keeping the punctuation and adding no extra '!' characters.","--shout can come before or after the name.","--shout without a name behaves like a missing name does today: usage message on stderr, exit 2.","'Shows up on the published docs site' means documenting it in docs/index.md, since that file is what the existing workflow publishes. The live site can only be checked after merge.","The request does not say how to implement it, for example whether src/greet.js gets a new export or the CLI uppercases the output. The builder decides."]}}